-- title:
--   Regularity of the special fibre at ordinary points of the Gauss branch
-- statement:
--   Let $q \ge 5$ be a prime and $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K \subseteq L(\!(T)\!)$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with perfect residue field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$ and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$, $j \ne 0$, be the element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, and let $\mathfrak{X} = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}(A,K,j)$ be the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ along their common refinement, with structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L(\!(T)\!)$ (the Gauss valuation ring). Let $z \in \mathfrak{X}$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section pulled back from $\varpi \in A$ along the structure morphism, assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$; assume $z$ is the image of a point $y$ of the chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j]$ whose prime ideal is maximal; assume there is a homomorphism $\varphi$ from that chart algebra to an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ such that $\varphi(j)$ does not lie in $\mathrm{ssJSet}_q(\Omega)$, i.e. it is not the case that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has trivial $q$-torsion; and assume that every element of the chart algebra lying in the set of nonunits of $W_0$ lies in $y$. Then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the local regularity statement for the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ over $A$, at a closed point of the $j$-finite chart which is ordinary (non-supersingular $j$-invariant) and lies on the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation. It feeds the construction of open neighbourhoods on which the map to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ is smooth, and the corresponding regularity statement at the points singled out as good.
